# Where the stress falls in the Russian words met most, written for this
# module rather than taken from any dictionary: one word or several to a
# line, small letters but for the stressed vowel, which is a capital. A word
# with ё needs no capital, since ё is stressed where it stands, and a word of
# one syllable needs no line.
#
# A word may be followed by = and how it is said where that is not how it is
# written: конЕчно=конЕшно.
#
# tools/module/stresswords.py reads this, asks a built engine how it stresses
# each word as the rules stand, and writes into main.dic only the words the
# rules get wrong, each as itself with the stress mark after its vowel. So a
# word the rules come to place right leaves main.dic by itself, and this file
# is the one to add to.

